class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> twoSum(vector<int>& nums, int target) {
        unordered_map<int, int> mp;

        for (int i = 0; i < nums.size(); i++) {
            int complement = target - nums[i];

            if (mp.find(complement) != mp.end())
                return {mp[complement], i};

            mp[nums[i]] = i;
        }

        return {};
    }
};
**Intuition:**  
For each element, find the value needed to reach the target.  
Use a hash map to quickly check if that value was already seen.

**Algorithm:**  
Traverse the array and calculate `target - nums[i]`.  
If the complement exists in the map, return both indices; otherwise store the current element.

**Complexity:**  
Time: **O(n)**  
Space: **O(n)**
